count level, not per tag; an account Pinterest cannot score yet carries &#x60;error&#x60; instead). Pinterest has no time-bounded counts, so &#x60;startTime&#x60;/&#x60;endTime&#x60; answer 400.  TikTok: per-event counts from &#x60;/pixel/event/stats/&#x60; (&#x60;total_count&#x60;, &#x60;browser_event_total_count&#x60;, &#x60;server_event_total_count&#x60;, &#x60;attributed_count&#x60;, &#x60;preview_count&#x60;), bucketed by UTC day. Defaults to the last 7 days; at most 30 days per request. &#x60;aggregation&#x60; is not accepted.  X Ads (platform &#x60;xads&#x60;): X has no event counts per pixel or event (only campaign-level conversion metrics). Each row is one web event tag with its &#x60;status&#x60; (TRACKING, UNVERIFIED, DORMANT), &#x60;lastTrackedTime&#x60; (unix seconds, null if never seen), &#x60;autoCreated&#x60; and, for events the site can fire, &#x60;siteEventId&#x60;. 
